{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BaHCVzyiRbMxa7td3toYuq","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The KIP that discusses a broker-side exception for rejecting oversized pushed client configuration is KIP-1324 \\\\\\\"Support client configuration observability\\\\\\\" [mail:a1a76025a895e9029a8c8b94]. As of May 5, 2026, the final exception class name decided was `ConfigTooLargeException` [mail:a1a76025a895e9029a8c8b94].\\\\n\\\\nSupporting facts in time order:\\\\n- On 2026-05-03, the exception was referred to as `ClientConfigTooLargeException`, mapping to a `CLIENT_CONFIG_TOO_LARGE` error code [mail:3c95b9de8b2aa4f6ed3bef47]. This was before the May 5 finalization.\\\\n- On 2026-05-05T15:09:46Z, Kirk True, replying to Mickael Maison on the dev@kafka.apache.org list, confirmed the final name as `ConfigTooLargeException` [mail:a1a76025a895e9029a8c8b94].\\\\n\\\\nWhat could not be determined: The github records search found no matching KIP or exception class name (the only \\\\\\\"oversized\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"config\\\\\\\" hits were unrelated, e.g., github:api:apache/kafka:pr-20149-closed on KAFKA-14405) [github:api:apache/kafka:pr-20149-closed]. The mail records provided the answer; no conflict remains.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:a1a76025a895e9029a8c8b94\\\",\\\"mail:3c95b9de8b2aa4f6ed3bef47\\\",\\\"github:api:apache/kafka:pr-20149-closed\\\",\\\"github:api:apache/kafka:comment-IC_kwDOACG9q88AAAABBJWIIw\\\",\\\"mail:6c643315a34fcdb22f25b861\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":118.285,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":14,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0093885,\\\"input_tokens\\\":226068,\\\"output_tokens\\\":24029}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"784f5b0d-d2d8-4216-94f3-ac1fa127ddb4","uuid":"59152c9e-4f2a-4594-a02f-99181ca37bf2","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:21:01.610Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"a